{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:46:27.183Z","data":{"turn":18,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_014dcJJNC3WAtY3W9Y1v155P\",\"name\":\"Agent\",\"input\":{\"description\":\"Analyze GigDetail.jsx XSS sink and review data flow\",\"subagent_type\":\"general-purpose\",\"prompt\":\"You are a security code analyst. Analyze the following files for XSS vulnerabilities. This is READ-ONLY analysis - do not modify any files.\\n\\nTarget application is at /repos/webvulnbench/\\n\\n1. Read the file `client/src/pages/GigDetail.jsx` - find the `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` usage at line 299. Read the full component to understand:\\n   - What data is passed to dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\n   - Where that data comes from (API calls, state, props)\\n   - Is there any sanitization applied before the render?\\n   - What is the exact render context?\\n\\n2. Read the reviews API endpoint at `src/reviews/reviews.controller.js` and `src/reviews/reviews.service.js` to understand:\\n   - How review comments are stored\\n   - Is any sanitization applied on input?\\n   - How are reviews retrieved for display?\\n   - What database fields are read back?\\n\\n3. Read `src/reviews/reviews.routes.js` to understand authentication requirements\\n\\nProvide a complete trace: POST /api/reviews (input) → database storage → GET API response → GigDetail.jsx dangerouslySetInnerHTML (output sink)\\n\\nInclude:\\n- Exact file:line for each step\\n- Any sanitization functions encountered\\n- The exact JS/JSX code at the sink\\n- Whether the data path confirms an unsanitized stored XSS vulnerability\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:46:27.183Z"}}
{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:46:34.468Z","data":{"turn":19,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01AeRz2ynS6wK7Yxhanv4moP\",\"name\":\"Agent\",\"input\":{\"description\":\"Analyze file upload XSS and Puppeteer HTML injection sinks\",\"subagent_type\":\"general-purpose\",\"prompt\":\"You are a security code analyst. Analyze these files for XSS vulnerabilities. This is READ-ONLY analysis - do not modify any files.\\n\\nTarget application is at /repos/webvulnbench/\\n\\n**Task 1: Unrestricted File Upload Analysis**\\nRead `src/middleware/upload.js` to understand:\\n- Which upload configurations have no fileFilter?\\n- What MIME types/extensions are accepted?\\n- Where are files stored (path)?\\n- How are files served back (static serving)?\\n\\nRead `src/index.js` to understand how `/uploads/` is served statically.\\n\\nRead `src/contracts/contracts.routes.js` and `src/messaging/messaging.routes.js` for the upload endpoints.\\n\\n**Task 2: Puppeteer HTML Injection Analysis**\\nRead `src/utils/pdf.js` (lines 55-76) to find:\\n- How are user-controlled values (display_name, milestone.title) interpolated into the HTML template?\\n- Is there any HTML encoding/escaping before interpolation?\\n- What is the exact template string?\\n\\nRead `src/contracts/contracts.service.js` to find where the invoice PDF is generated and what data is passed to the PDF generator.\\n\\nRead `src/contracts/contracts.controller.js` to understand the invoice endpoint flow.\\n\\n**Task 3: Email HTML Injection Analysis**\\nRead `src/contracts/contracts.service.js` lines 296-299 and 386-387 to find:\\n- How are milestone.title and reason interpolated into the email HTML?\\n- Is there any sanitization?\\n- What is the exact email template?\\n\\nProvide detailed findings for each task including file:line references and exact code snippets.\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:46:34.468Z"}}
{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:46:41.278Z","data":{"turn":20,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01DBsF88JKany2a5L8FpCEiV\",\"name\":\"Agent\",\"input\":{\"description\":\"Scan frontend code for additional DOM-based XSS sinks\",\"subagent_type\":\"general-purpose\",\"prompt\":\"You are a security code analyst. Scan the frontend React codebase for XSS vulnerabilities. This is READ-ONLY analysis - do not modify any files.\\n\\nTarget application frontend is at /repos/webvulnbench/client/src/\\n\\n**Search for all potential XSS sinks:**\\n\\n1. Search for `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` across all frontend files - list each occurrence with file:line and what data is passed to it.\\n\\n2. Search for `innerHTML` assignments in JavaScript/JSX files.\\n\\n3. Search for `document.write` usage.\\n\\n4. Search for `eval(` usage.\\n\\n5. Search for URL parameters being read: `location.search`, `location.hash`, `URLSearchParams`, `window.location` - where are these values used?\\n\\n6. Search for `href` attributes being set dynamically from user data - could lead to javascript: URL injection.\\n\\n7. Look at the React Router implementation - are there any route params rendered without encoding?\\n\\n8. Check if any components render user profile data (display_name, bio, username) - are these rendered safely or via dangerouslySetInnerHTML?\\n\\n9. Look at the messaging components - how are message contents rendered?\\n\\n10. Check the gig listing and detail pages for any other unsafe rendering.\\n\\nFor each finding, provide:\\n- File path and line number\\n- The exact code\\n- What data flows into the sink\\n- Whether any sanitization is present\\n\\nUse grep/search tools to be comprehensive. List ALL files in client/src/pages/ and client/src/components/ first.\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:46:41.278Z"}}
