{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:55:24.811Z","data":{"turn":66,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01251Ano8BFMxdoLG3ufWX7q\",\"name\":\"Agent\",\"input\":{\"description\":\"Trace attachment_url and deliverable_url data flows\",\"subagent_type\":\"general-purpose\",\"prompt\":\"You are a security code analyst. READ-ONLY analysis - do not modify files.\\n\\nTarget: /repos/webvulnbench/\\n\\n**Task 1: Trace `attachment_url` in messaging**\\n\\n1. Read `src/messaging/messaging.service.js` - how is `attachment_url` set when a message is created? Is it a URL to a stored file? Can an attacker supply a `javascript:` scheme URL?\\n\\n2. Read `src/messaging/messaging.controller.js` - how is the message creation endpoint handled? What happens with uploaded files? Is there any URL validation?\\n\\n3. Look at the messaging routes to understand the message schema.\\n\\n**Task 2: Trace `deliverable_url` in contracts**\\n\\n1. Read `src/contracts/contracts.service.js` - how is `deliverable_url` set when a milestone is submitted? Is it a path to an uploaded file or a user-provided URL?\\n\\n2. Read `src/contracts/contracts.controller.js` - the submitDeliverable handler - what input does it take?\\n\\n**Task 3: Profile page - website field**\\n\\n1. Read `client/src/pages/Profile.jsx` - is there a `website` field rendered as an `href` link? Is there any validation that it's an http/https URL?\\n\\n2. Read `src/users/users.service.js` - does PUT /api/users/:id validate the `website` field format (i.e., require http/https prefix)?\\n\\nFor each finding, provide:\\n- Exact file:line references\\n- Whether the URL value can be attacker-controlled (e.g., can they set it to `javascript:alert(1)`)\\n- Whether there's any sanitization/validation\\n\\nThe goal is to determine if any of these `href` attributes can be set to `javascript:` URLs by an attacker, constituting a DOM-based XSS.\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:55:24.811Z"}}
