{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T08:07:44.152Z","data":{"turn":185,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01MqEhg8pf22c8zhJjdrtq3o\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"SESSION_COOKIE=\\\"connect.sid=s%3AsKIN8xwQFowr94V5EV173ZEzad9j6-lN.zNdhUR4zUO43jPl3L%2F8jK0IdxPduSaMs9R4%2B4WMH4lI\\\"\\n\\n# Use session cookie to call API directly to create gig (multipart)\\ncurl -s -X POST \\\"http://host.docker.internal:3000/api/gigs\\\" \\\\\\n  -H \\\"Cookie: $SESSION_COOKIE\\\" \\\\\\n  -F \\\"title=Professional Web Development Services XSS Test\\\" \\\\\\n  -F \\\"category=web-development\\\" \\\\\\n  -F \\\"description=Professional web development services including React Node.js and database design\\\" \\\\\\n  -F 'tags=[\\\"web-development\\\",\\\"nodejs\\\",\\\"react\\\"]' \\\\\\n  -F 'pricing_tiers=[{\\\"name\\\":\\\"basic\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Basic Package\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Complete web dev package\\\",\\\"price\\\":5000,\\\"delivery_days\\\":7,\\\"revisions\\\":3}]' \\\\\\n  -F 'requirements=[]' \\\\\\n  -F 'faqs=[]' 2>&1 | head -20\",\"description\":\"Create gig via API with session cookie\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}","timestamp":"2026-04-08T08:07:44.152Z"}}
{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T08:07:58.265Z","data":{"turn":186,"content":"{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"The issue is with how Mongoose handles JSON arrays sent as multipart form data. The JSON string `[\\\"web-development\\\",\\\"nodejs\\\",\\\"react\\\"]` is being interpreted incorrectly - it seems there's an issue with how the array is serialized.\\n\\nLet me check the gig service/model to understand the correct format for multipart form submission.\\n\\nWait, looking at the error more carefully:\\n- `tags.undefined: Cast to [undefined] failed for value '[\\\"web-development\\\",\\\"nodejs\\\",\\\"react\\\"]'` → this means when tags is a string that looks like `[\\\"...\\\",\\\"...\\\"]`, it's being parsed but something is failing\\n\\nAlso: `tags: Cast to [undefined] failed for value \\\"[]\\\" (type string) at path \\\"tags.6\\\"` → this is strange. \\n\\nThe `tags.6` path is revealing - it looks like multer is parsing the form data and treating each element in the JSON array as a separate field, so I'm getting tags[0] through tags[6] instead of a single tags field with an array value. The form fields are being sent as strings rather than parsed JSON, and somehow there are extra array elements being created—the error mentions `tags.6` which suggests a 7th element exists. Let me step back and examine the Gig model's validation rules directly instead of continuing to debug the API submission.\",\"signature\":\"\"}","timestamp":"2026-04-08T08:07:58.265Z"}}
