{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T08:08:13.973Z","data":{"turn":191,"content":"{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"I can see how the form data is sent:\\n1. `tags` is sent as `JSON.stringify(tagsArray)` → so the value is like `[\\\"web-development\\\",\\\"nodejs\\\",\\\"react\\\"]`\\n2. `pricing` is sent as `JSON.stringify(pricingPayload)` → the full pricing object as JSON string\\n3. Images are appended as actual files\\n\\nBut the server-side controller code does:\\n```js\\nif (typeof gigData.pricing_tiers === 'string') {\\n  gigData.pricing_tiers = JSON.parse(gigData.pricing_tiers);\\n\\n\\n```\\n\\nThere's a field name mismatch — the client sends `pricing` but the controller is looking for `pricing_tiers`. Plus, the client structures pricing as an object keyed by tier names (basic, standard, premium), while the Gig model expects `pricing_tiers` as an array. I need to check how the model actually expects this data to be formatted.\",\"signature\":\"\"}","timestamp":"2026-04-08T08:08:13.973Z"}}
