{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T08:15:40.048Z","data":{"turn":252,"content":"{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Still \\\"Validation failed\\\". The form is being submitted but the server is returning 400. Let me understand why the validation is failing at a deeper level.\\n\\nActually, let me try a completely different approach. Let me try directly writing to the MongoDB via a raw TCP connection with the MongoDB wire protocol. Since I can connect to MongoDB on port 27017, I can try to insert a document directly.\\n\\nThe MongoDB wire protocol uses a binary format. But it's complex to implement from scratch.\\n\\nActually, wait - let me look at this from yet another angle. The mongos/mongod on port 27017 has NO auth (from recon). \\n\\nLet me reconsider the gig endpoint instead. The route uses `gigImageUpload.array('images', 5)` middleware which only processes multipart form data, so if I send JSON instead, multer will skip it and express.json() will parse the body normally. Let me test whether the endpoint works with a plain JSON request.\",\"signature\":\"\"}","timestamp":"2026-04-08T08:15:40.048Z"}}
