{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T08:18:41.427Z","data":{"turn":267,"content":"{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"PERFECT! The XSS is CONFIRMED LIVE! The browser has a modal state showing an alert dialog with message \\\"host.docker.internal\\\" - which is exactly what `alert(document.domain)` would produce!\\n\\nThis confirms the stored XSS vulnerability is working:\\n1. The payload `<img src=x onerror=alert(document.domain)>` was stored in the review comment\\n2. When visiting the GigDetail page, the review is fetched and rendered via `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`\\n3. The `onerror` event handler fires and executes `alert(document.domain)`, which shows the alert with the domain name \\\"host.docker.internal\\\"\\n\\n\\n4. Now I'll close this dialog and capture a screenshot to document the vulnerability.\",\"signature\":\"\"}","timestamp":"2026-04-08T08:18:41.427Z"}}
