{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T08:18:59.695Z","data":{"turn":273,"content":"{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"The XSS was confirmed via the modal alert dialog that appeared on the gig detail page. The `alert(document.domain)` executed with the value \\\"host.docker.internal\\\", confirming code execution in the browser context.\\n\\nNow let me move on to:\\n1. Test the file upload XSS (Upload HTML file to /uploads/)\\n2. Analyze other sinks\\n3. Generate deliverables\\n\\nLet me also note the cookie security for the session. The recon said:\\n- `Cookie: connect.sid` - `httpOnly: true`, no `sameSite` attribute, `secure` only in production\\n\\n\\n- From the index.js: `httpOnly: true`\\n\\nSince `httpOnly: true` is set on the session cookie, `document.cookie` won't expose the session cookie in the XSS context. But if there's a JWT stored in localStorage, that would be accessible to the payload, so I need to check whether the application stores any tokens there.\",\"signature\":\"\"}","timestamp":"2026-04-08T08:18:59.695Z"}}
